# Build output
#
# tools\build.ps1 assembles the runnable application here (RyukinLedger.exe,
# irminsul.exe and a copy of assets\).  It is regenerated on every build, so
# there is nothing in it worth versioning -- releases are published from it,
# not committed from it.
dist/

# .NET
#
# bin\ and obj\ are matched at any depth: the application project lives in a
# subfolder today and may move.
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/

# Rust
#
# The capture core's build tree.  Half a gigabyte of object files, and it
# contains absolute paths from whatever machine built it.
target/

# OS and editors
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Local maintenance notes
#
# UPDATING.md is the handover runbook for the next game or upstream update: the
# one constant that changes with a game version, where it lives, how to verify
# it against this machine's logs.  It is notes for whoever works on the project
# here, not part of what is shipped, so it stays out of the repository.
UPDATING.md

# NOT ignored, on purpose:
#
#   src/irminsul/.cargo/config.toml   static CRT linking: part of the build, not a
#                                 local preference
#   src/irminsul/keys/gi.json         the initial session keys, embedded in the
#                                 binary with include_bytes!
#   assets/                       the artwork; the application copies it into
#                                 the output folder
#   docs/                         screenshots the README renders
